; Semantic schema10 retention over the actual held metadata entry.
; The work ledger has one row per physical allocator extent. Each call clears
; one row, reads/copies one physical unit, verifies one bounded format step,
; or decodes one actual entry. No cache hit stands in for authentication.
; The current served run writer reserves a fresh physical page for each
; promoted tree page. Exact shared full roots/filter identities are supported;
; shared subtrees under distinct roots and repeated child edges explicitly
; refuse. General shared-subtree DAG traversal remains a separate frontier.
(in-package "ACL2")
(include-book "std/util/bstar" :dir :system)
(include-book "checkpoint-metadata-retention")
(include-book "checkpoint-semantic-page")
(include-book "checkpoint-boot")
(include-book "recovery")
